WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Taika, it is so wonderful
to see you again.

00:00:02.369 --> 00:00:03.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this is one of my
favorite books

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:06.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you're doing
these YouTube readings of.

00:00:06.473 --> 00:00:09.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
How did you come about picking
"James and the Giant Peach

00:00:09.109 --> 00:00:13.713
and what made you want
to start reading it with people?

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:17.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Um, well, hi.
-Hi.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:22.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I'm doing some
Roald Dahl stuff

00:00:22.389 --> 00:00:23.323 line:92%
with Netflix at the moment

00:00:23.323 --> 00:00:26.826 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we're turning a bunch
of his books into animations

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:31.097
And just through my relationship
with the Dahl Story Compan

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:35.068
and the family and everything,
they -- it was their initiativ

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:39.406 size:75% position:38%
just to do something
to raise some money.

00:00:39.406 --> 00:00:42.909
And we thought it was just
a really nice idea to --

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:45.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
yeah, to have a series
of readings over the natural -

00:00:45.345 --> 00:00:49.249
of a whole book, something tha
you could tune into each week.

00:00:49.249 --> 00:00:52.952
And it just feels like a nic
thing to do with your kids

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:55.121 align:start size:94% position:6%
and just, you know,
for people to sit around.

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:55.755 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Almost like a radio show

00:00:55.755 --> 00:00:58.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
but with some
really blurry pictures.

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:02.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then it just sort of built
from there,

00:01:02.462 --> 00:01:03.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
just getting more
and more people on board,

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:08.168 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's been quite a long tim
since I've read that book.

00:01:08.168 --> 00:01:10.904 line:92%
So when I started reading it

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:13.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just kind of forgotten
it had been so long.

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:14.707 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so it was really like
reading it

00:01:14.707 --> 00:01:15.975 line:92%
for the first time for me.

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:19.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm pretty sure the only time
I have read it,

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:21.381 line:92%
it was read to me by my mother

00:01:21.381 --> 00:01:25.718
So I actually am a little
disappointed at how my mom

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:29.989 align:start size:94% position:6%
did not pull in any celebrit
friends when she read it.

00:01:29.989 --> 00:01:31.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, you know,
this is sort of --

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:34.294 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, a big lesson learned
with what we're doing,

00:01:34.294 --> 00:01:35.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think,
for most parents out there

00:01:35.695 --> 00:01:38.932 align:start size:94% position:6%
just to befriend lots
and lots of celebrities.

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:40.166 size:81% position:41% line:92%
This is the first time

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:42.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've met most
of those people, by the way.

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:45.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You did get a pretty
impressive group.

00:01:45.205 --> 00:01:48.475 align:start size:94% position:6%
Meryl Strip -- Meryl Streep.
[ Laughs ]

00:01:48.475 --> 00:01:49.342 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-And Meryl Strip.

00:01:49.342 --> 00:01:50.877 align:start size:94% position:6%
We've got to get rid
of Meryl Strip.

00:01:50.877 --> 00:01:53.446 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, Meryl Strip you
never want around children

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:55.281 align:start size:94% position:6%
She is --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:58.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Very different episode.
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:58.284 --> 00:01:59.886 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Camilla Parker Bowles.

00:01:59.886 --> 00:02:02.655 line:92%
How does that come about?

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:04.424 size:88% position:44%
-I'm still very nervous
even talking about that.

00:02:04.424 --> 00:02:07.627 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm not even sure how
I'm supposed to address it

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:08.461 line:92%
There were a lot of rules.

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:13.566
Like, okay, basically, you know,
you can't look her in the eye,

00:02:13.566 --> 00:02:17.537 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you've got to call
her certain things.

00:02:17.537 --> 00:02:20.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
Couldn't come in and say,
"Hey, Cami."

00:02:20.173 --> 00:02:21.207 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Right.

00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:23.877 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I mean
she was really lovely.

00:02:23.877 --> 00:02:25.211 align:start size:94% position:6%
But that was probably
the most subdued

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:27.213 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'd been in all the readings
-Yeah.

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:28.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was on that.
-Congratulations.

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:34.420 align:start size:94% position:6%
You just received an honor
from the Queen of New Zealand.

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:35.388 line:92%
I hope I'm stating that right.

00:02:35.388 --> 00:02:38.158 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm right in with royalty
at the moment.

00:02:38.158 --> 00:02:39.425 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Me and the crown.

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:40.827 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Yes, that's right.

00:02:40.827 --> 00:02:42.562 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean there's so many letters
attached to it.

00:02:42.562 --> 00:02:48.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, O-B --
an Order of Merit.

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:51.104 size:81% position:41%
You become an Officer
of the Order of Merit.

00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:52.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it's something
I've been doing for a while.

00:02:52.539 --> 00:02:55.241 align:start size:94% position:6%
I like to think the Queen
just googled all her subject

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:58.811
in the colonies and said,
"Oh, what about that one?"

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:02.048 align:start size:94% position:6%
What makes it good
is that it's --

00:03:02.048 --> 00:03:03.449 line:92%
you're recommended by people

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:05.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
in your country,
you know, for those things

00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:10.423 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then it goes up top,
and I guess she just sort of -

00:03:10.423 --> 00:03:12.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
yes.
-Well, that's a nice honor

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:16.462
Another nice honor, of course,
we spoke right before the Oscars

00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:17.664 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
last time we spoke.

00:03:17.664 --> 00:03:21.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were nominated for and the
you won the Oscar

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:24.137 align:start size:94% position:6%
for writing the screenplay
for "Jojo Rabbit."

00:03:24.137 --> 00:03:25.538 line:92%
I have to assume to some degre

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:28.007 size:75% position:38%
because of the press
you did on our show.

00:03:28.007 --> 00:03:29.042 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, that's --
-Yes, that's right.

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:33.046 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think I got a lot
of points with the little card

00:03:33.046 --> 00:03:33.746 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
that I made you.

00:03:33.746 --> 00:03:37.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You made a beautiful drawing.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:38.051 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-You're a handy guy.

00:03:38.051 --> 00:03:40.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
I also want to get back
to "Jojo Rabbit,"

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:42.388 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you've been
making some incredible --

00:03:42.388 --> 00:03:43.289 line:92%
would you call them puppets?

00:03:43.289 --> 00:03:46.292 align:start size:94% position:6%
What are you making?
-Yeah, I've been sewing.

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:49.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've been trying to teach
my kids how to sew.

00:03:49.095 --> 00:03:52.732 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've been a sewer, you know,
since way back,

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:54.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they're not
really interested.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
All they do is just say,
"Make me a snake.

00:03:56.236 --> 00:03:59.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
Make me a bear."
So I just do all the work.

00:03:59.639 --> 00:04:00.440 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And it's a lovely thing.

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:01.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think, you know,
one of the things

00:04:01.608 --> 00:04:03.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
I can take away from just
the lockdown at least

00:04:03.843 --> 00:04:07.780
is spending a lot more tim
with the family and with my kids

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:10.817 align:start size:94% position:6%
and being able to try
and keep them entertained

00:04:10.817 --> 00:04:14.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
by really exciting things
like sewing.

00:04:14.254 --> 00:04:14.654 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:04:14.654 --> 00:04:17.757 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know what would be
great today?

00:04:17.757 --> 00:04:20.627 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, is it two girls
4 and 8?

00:04:20.627 --> 00:04:22.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that right?
-That's right, yeah.

00:04:22.295 --> 00:04:28.534
-And they're not impressed
with your non-sewing work?

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:29.469 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
They don't --

00:04:29.469 --> 00:04:31.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
they don't really care
for anything else I've done.

00:04:31.838 --> 00:04:34.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
They've been on all the sets
of all my films.

00:04:34.674 --> 00:04:36.009
I think it was just the last one
they were on,

00:04:36.009 --> 00:04:39.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
probably like the fourth
or fifth film they've been on,

00:04:39.379 --> 00:04:40.880 line:92%
where they got an inkling

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:43.283
that I could make some decisions
on a film

00:04:43.283 --> 00:04:47.020 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that I might be someone,
you know, important.

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:50.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
But usually -- my 8-year-old
likes to troll me

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:55.061 align:start size:94% position:6%
and say things like, "Oh, Dad,
I really love 'Iron Man.'

00:04:55.061 --> 00:04:56.529 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Great film."

00:04:56.529 --> 00:04:59.165 align:start size:94% position:6%
Knowing full well
I didn't make it.

00:04:59.165 --> 00:05:02.168 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then the 4-year-old
is at that age

00:05:02.168 --> 00:05:05.705 align:start size:94% position:6%
where she just gets
in your head, you know.

00:05:05.705 --> 00:05:08.708
You know, they understand
the psychology of men,

00:05:08.708 --> 00:05:10.376 line:92%
and they start to sort of

00:05:10.376 --> 00:05:13.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
just tearing you down
psychologically.

00:05:13.746 --> 00:05:15.715 line:92%
So I'm dealing with that.

00:05:15.715 --> 00:05:19.986
-What was your process
of writing the screenplay

00:05:19.986 --> 00:05:20.720 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
for "Jojo Rabbit"

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:23.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
compared to other times
that you've written scripts?

00:05:23.523 --> 00:05:24.691 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Was it different?

00:05:24.691 --> 00:05:27.460 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was very different
in that --

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:29.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I really hope
I capture it again

00:05:29.395 --> 00:05:30.830 line:92%
where it was just quite easy

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:32.365 size:78% position:39%
That's the first time
I've written a script

00:05:32.365 --> 00:05:33.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
from page
one all the way through.

00:05:33.633 --> 00:05:37.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, usually I start
at the end.

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:38.571 line:92%
Okay, this will be a good end.

00:05:38.571 --> 00:05:41.507
And maybe something --
this is at the beginning.

00:05:41.507 --> 00:05:42.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then a couple of things
in the middle,

00:05:42.608 --> 00:05:45.578
and I try and glue them al
together and make it make sense.

00:05:45.578 --> 00:05:47.880 align:start size:94% position:6%
But that one flowed
quite easily,

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:51.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'm scared that
that won't happen again.

00:05:51.784 --> 00:05:53.886 size:81% position:41%
-I know you're working
on a "Star Wars" film.

00:05:53.886 --> 00:05:55.922 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're working on another
"Thor" film.

00:05:55.922 --> 00:05:59.826
Obviously you have to fit
into pre-existing worlds.

00:05:59.826 --> 00:06:01.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
You obviously have
cracked it before.

00:06:01.427 --> 00:06:04.163 align:start size:94% position:6%
I thought "Thor: Ragnarok"
was fantastic.

00:06:04.163 --> 00:06:06.966
Is it nice to have that
structure in place of the worlds

00:06:06.966 --> 00:06:08.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
that have been built
before you start working,

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:10.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
or is it a little --
-Yeah, it is.

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:12.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
It sort of feels --
I mean "Thor" feels

00:06:12.805 --> 00:06:13.906 line:92%
like an adaptation of something.

00:06:13.906 --> 00:06:15.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, you're using
source material.

00:06:15.608 --> 00:06:18.244 align:start size:94% position:6%
And for me it was a lot easier
coming in, "Okay.

00:06:18.244 --> 00:06:19.946 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't have to make up
any characters.

00:06:19.946 --> 00:06:20.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is great."
-Right.

00:06:20.913 --> 00:06:23.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I just have to make them
do funny things.

00:06:23.883 --> 00:06:26.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, who knows
with "Star Wars"

00:06:26.719 --> 00:06:28.121 line:92%
exactly what the tone will be.

00:06:28.121 --> 00:06:29.889 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
But similar thing.

00:06:29.889 --> 00:06:34.560
There's -- Well, with "Jojo" i
was also an established world.

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:39.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, that's true.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:06:39.532 --> 00:06:42.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
But definitely on somethin
like the Marvel films,

00:06:42.235 --> 00:06:44.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's a really fun
environment to work in,

00:06:44.604 --> 00:06:46.139 size:78% position:39%
because you can look
at the comic and say,

00:06:46.139 --> 00:06:48.441 line:92%
"What about this character?"

00:06:48.441 --> 00:06:48.941 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:06:48.941 --> 00:06:51.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They're like, "Okay,
give it a go."

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:52.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well it certainly paid of
last time.

00:06:52.912 --> 00:06:55.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
They made a great choice
with you at the helm.

00:06:55.715 --> 00:06:57.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's always just a delight
to talk to you.

00:06:57.784 --> 00:06:59.685 align:start size:94% position:6%
Stay healthy and love
to your family.

00:06:59.685 --> 00:07:01.788 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thanks, mate.
Lovely to see you.

